{:edb/db-before-t 1795 :edb/db-after-t 1796 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535108 50 #inst "2026-10-08T17:03:51.781Z" 13194139535108 true] [17592186128924 1100 "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} xy\\ \\!e^{x+y}\\ \\textrm d A$ over the rectangle $R= [0,1] \\times [1,2]$." 13194139535108 false] [17592186128924 1100 "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} xy\\ \\!e^{x+y}\\ \\textrm d A$ over the rectangle $R= [0,1] \\times [1,2].$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186128924 1145 "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\iint\\limits_{R} xy \\\\ e^{x+y}\\: \\textrm d A &= \\iint\\limits_{R} \\Big(x\\ \\! e^x \\Big)\\Big(y\\ \\! e^{y} \\Big) \\textrm d A \\\\[5pt] &= \\left(\\int_0^1x \\\\ e^{x} \\ \\textrm d x\\right)\\left(\\int_1^2 y \\ \\!e^{y} \\ \\textrm d y\\right) \\\\[5pt] &= \\Big[x\\ \\!e^x-e^x\\Big]_0^1 \\cdot \\Big[y\\ \\!e^y-e^y\\Big]_1^2 \\\\[5pt] &= \\Big(e^1-e^1 - \\left(0-e^0\\right)\\Big) \\cdot \\Big(2e^2-e^2 - \\left(e^1-e^1\\right) \\Big) \\\\[5pt] &= 1\\cdot e^2 \\\\[5pt] &= e^2 \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535108 false] [17592186128924 1145 "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\iint\\limits_{R}  xy\\  e^{x+y}\\: \\textrm d A &= \\iint\\limits_{R} \\Big( x\\ \\! e^x \\Big)\\Big( y\\ \\! e^{y} \\Big) \\textrm d A\\[5pt]\n&= \\left(\\int_0^1x\\  e^{x}  \\ \\textrm d x\\right)\\left( \\int_1^2 y \\ \\!e^{y} \\ \\textrm d y\\right)\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= \\Big[x\\ \\!e^x-e^x\\Big]_0^1 \\cdot  \\Big[y\\ \\!e^y-e^y\\Big]_1^2\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &=  \\Big(e^1-e^1 - \\left(0-e^0\\right)\\Big) \\cdot \\Big(2e^2-e^2 - \\left(e^1-e^1\\right) \\Big)\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= 1\\cdot e^2\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= e^2\n}\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186128925 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} \\left(x^2-y^2 +3\\right)  \\textrm d A,$  where $R= [-1,3] \\times [2, 4].$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186128925 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} \\left(x^2-y^2 +3\\right) \\textrm d A$, where $R= [-1,3] \\times [2, 4]$." 13194139535108 false] [17592186128925 1145 "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(R)(x^{2} - y^{2} + 3)dA &= ∬_(R)x^{2}dA - ∬_(R)y^{2}dA + ∬_(R)3dA\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's evaluate each of the three integrals.\n\n- The function under the first integral is independent of $y$. So, we have\n$∬_(R)x^{2}dA|= (4 - 2)∫_{-1}^{3}x^{2}dx; = 2 \\cdot \\frac{x^{3}}{3} \\mid _{-1}^{3}; = 2(\\frac{27}{3} + \\frac{1}{3}); = \\frac{56}{3}$.\n- The function under the second integral is independent of $x$. So, we have\n$∬_(R)y^{2}dA|= (3 - (-1))∫_{2}^{4}y^{2}dy; = 4∫_{2}^{4}y^{2}dy; = 4 \\cdot \\frac{y^{3}}{3} \\mid _{2}^{4}; = \\frac{4}{3}4^{3} - \\frac{4}{3}2^{3}; = \\frac{224}{3}$.\n- The function under the third integral is a constant, so we have\n$∬_(R)3dA = 3Area(R) = 3 \\cdot (2 \\cdot 4) = 24$.\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n∬_(R)(x^{2} - y^{2} + 3)dA = \\frac{56}{3} - \\frac{224}{3} + 24 =-32\n$$" 13194139535108 false] [17592186128925 1145 "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+3)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}3\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's evaluate each of the three integrals.\n\n- The function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(4-2){\\int }_{-1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{27}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(3-(-1)){\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{4}^{3}-\\frac{4}{3}{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{224}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function under the third integral is a constant, so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}3\\,\\text{d}A=3\\,\\text{Area}(R)=3\\cdot (2\\cdot 4)=24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}A=\\frac{56}{3}-\\frac{224}{3}+24=-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186128926 1100 "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A$, where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/assets/d96ec9ab40f8f1cadd6d2492dddcc0090f766b72e9c7fdb659e3b2f7f39fce0d.png)\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186128926 1100 "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A$, where\n\n${2,\\begin{vmatrix}if0 < x < 2,-1 < y < 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{xy + x + y + 1},\\end{vmatrix}if0 < x < 2, 0 < y < 1$,\nand $R$ is the domain of $f$." 13194139535108 false] [17592186128926 1145 "First, notice that we have\n\n$$\nR = R_1 \\cup R_2\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nR_1= (0,2) \\times (-1,0)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nR_2= (0,2) \\times (0,1)\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\iint\\limits_{R} f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A &= \\iint\\limits_{R_1} 2 \\ \\textrm d A + \\iint\\limits_{R_2} \\dfrac{1}{xy+x+y+1} \\ \\textrm d A \\\\[5pt] &= 2\\iint\\limits_{R_1} \\textrm d A + \\iint\\limits_{R_2} \\dfrac{1}{(x+1)(y+1)} \\ \\textrm d A \\\\[5pt] &= 2(2-0)(0-(-1)) + \\Bigg(\\int_0^2 \\dfrac{1}{x+1} \\ \\textrm d x \\Bigg) \\Bigg(\\int_0^1 \\dfrac{1}{y+1}\\ \\textrm d y \\Bigg) \\\\[5pt] &= 4 + \\Big[\\ln(x+1)\\Big]_0^2 \\cdot \\Big[\\ln(y+1)\\Big]_0^1 \\\\[5pt] &= 4+ \\ln 3\\ln 2. \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535108 false] [17592186128926 1145 "First, notice that we have $R = R_1 \\cup R_2,$ where $R_1= (0,2) \\times (-1,0)$ and $R_2= (0,2) \\times (0,1).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\iint\\limits_{R}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A &= \\iint\\limits_{R_1} 2 \\ \\textrm d A + \\iint\\limits_{R_2}    \\dfrac{1}{xy+x+y+1} \\ \\textrm d A\\[5pt]\n&= 2\\iint\\limits_{R_1} \\textrm d A\n+ \\iint\\limits_{R_2}  \\dfrac{1}{(x+1)(y+1)} \\ \\textrm d A\\[5pt]\n&= 2(2-0)(0-(-1)) + \\Bigg( \\int_0^2 \\dfrac{1}{x+1} \\ \\textrm d x \\Bigg) \\Bigg( \\int_0^1 \\dfrac{1}{y+1}\\ \\textrm d y \\Bigg) \\[5pt]\n&= 4 + \\Big[\\ln(x+1)\\Big]_0^2  \\cdot \\Big[\\ln(y+1)\\Big]_0^1\\[5pt] \n&= 4+ \\ln 3\\ln 2.\n}\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186128942 1100 "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{C}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A = 8,\n\\qquad\n\\iint\\limits_{D}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A = -5,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{C \\cup D}  3f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A.\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186128942 1100 "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n$\\iint\\limits_{C} f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A = 8, \\qquad \\iint\\limits_{D} f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A = -5$,\nfind the value of\n$\\iint\\limits_{C \\cup D} 3f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A$." 13194139535108 false] [17592186128942 1145 "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(C∪D)3f(x, y)dA &= 3∬_(C∪D)f(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= 3(∬_(C)f(x, y)dA + ∬_(D)f(x, y)dA) \\\\\n&= 3(8 + (-5)) \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535108 false] [17592186128942 1145 "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}3f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =3{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =3(8+(-5)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186129105 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331635 13194139535108 true] [17592186129105 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331642 13194139535108 true] [17592186129105 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331697 13194139535108 true] [17592186129105 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331704 13194139535108 true] [17592186129106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331711 13194139535108 true] [17592186129106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331718 13194139535108 true] [17592186129106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331725 13194139535108 true] [17592186129106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331746 13194139535108 true] [17592186129106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331753 13194139535108 true] [17592186129107 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331663 13194139535108 true] [17592186129107 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331670 13194139535108 true] [17592186129107 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331677 13194139535108 true] [17592186129107 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331684 13194139535108 true] [17592186129107 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331760 13194139535108 true] [17592186129123 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331649 13194139535108 true] [17592186129123 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331656 13194139535108 true] [17592186129123 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331732 13194139535108 true] [17592186129123 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331739 13194139535108 true] [17592186129782 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535108 true] [17592186129782 1100 "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{ }{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[0,\\pi ]\\times [0,1].$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186129782 1100 "Evaluate the double integral $∬_(R)\\sin xe^{y}dA$ over the rectangle $R = [0, π] \\cdot [0, 1]$." 13194139535108 false] [17592186129782 1145 "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{ }{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{ }({e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)\\cdot ({e}^{1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =-(-1-1)\\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =2(e-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186129810 1017 #edb/ref 17592186128654 13194139535108 false] [17592186129810 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331691 13194139535108 true] [17592186129810 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535108 true] [17592186129810 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/assets/ed0be2aca8d43d733e91f3a8feaaca0649957dcbd516a8218b1e7dea136170d8.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x, & (x,y)\\in S, \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in T, \\\\ {x}^{2}y, & (x,y)\\in U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186129810 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2000/Source/Images/q-80452.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x, y)$ be defined as\n$f(x, y) = {x,\\begin{vmatrix}(x, y) ∈ S, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}(x, y) ∈ T,; x^{2}y, \\mid (x, y) ∈ U$.\nThen,\n$∬_(R)f(x, y)dA =$" 13194139535108 false] [17592186129810 1145 "First, notice that the domain $R$ can be represented as a union of three sub-domains, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =S\\cup T\\cup U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{S}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}0\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331635 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331636 13194139535108 true] [17592186331635 1089 "q-129936" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331635 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535108 true] [17592186331635 1100 "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{{y}^{2}+1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,e]\\times [0,3].$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331635 1113 #uuid "872f93f5-8409-5a4d-bae6-2b36bd1649e0" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331635 1145 "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{{y}^{2}+1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x})({y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}({y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot [\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+3) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331637 13194139535108 true] [17592186331636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331638 13194139535108 true] [17592186331636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331639 13194139535108 true] [17592186331636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331640 13194139535108 true] [17592186331636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331641 13194139535108 true] [17592186331636 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535108 true] [17592186331636 1041 "selection" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331636 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331637 13194139535108 true] [17592186331636 1110 #uuid "e843a88b-3377-5f11-879e-da4431c7a178" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331637 1034 "12" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331637 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331637 1111 #uuid "065ad1df-9aa1-5a78-a9b9-15d291248fb4" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331638 1034 "e+6" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331638 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331638 1111 #uuid "364b9c98-896f-5017-b067-62e3f7940078" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331639 1034 "3" 13194139535108 t