592186331711 1113 #uuid "654ce247-5ae0-50de-879f-ff6be0880366" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331711 1145 "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(2+2x-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is a constant, so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}A=2\\,\\text{Area}(R)=2\\cdot (3\\cdot 2)=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}A & =(2-0){\\int }_{0}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot [{x}^{2}]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =2({3}^{2}-(0)^{2}) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the third integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}A & =(3-0){\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3\\cdot [{y}^{3}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =3({2}^{3}-{0}^{3}) \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(2+2x-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A=12+18-24=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331713 13194139535108 true] [17592186331712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331714 13194139535108 true] [17592186331712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331715 13194139535108 true] [17592186331712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331716 13194139535108 true] [17592186331712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331717 13194139535108 true] [17592186331712 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535108 true] [17592186331712 1041 "selection" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331712 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331715 13194139535108 true] [17592186331712 1110 #uuid "950f08cb-58ec-532b-b7f6-946277e6b610" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331713 1034 "12" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331713 1111 #uuid "3c736a60-846e-5be0-b49b-bb4f23bcc855" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331714 1