 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331738 1111 #uuid "cf39364c-de01-54e0-99c3-c1f890e0ab82" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331739 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331740 13194139535108 true] [17592186331739 1089 "q-80661" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331739 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535108 true] [17592186331739 1100 "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\\frac{1}{2},\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\\frac{3}{2},\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}\\frac{f(x,y)}{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331739 1113 #uuid "d34b0049-3b85-5ba9-bbfe-6ab88f4f0f19" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331739 1145 "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}\\frac{f(x,y)}{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331740 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331741 13194139535108 true] [17592186331740 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331742 13194139535108 true] [17592186331740 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331743 13194139535108 true] [17592186331740 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331744 13194139535108 true] [17592186331740 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331745 13194139535108 true] [17592186331740 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535108 true] [17592186331740 1041 "selection" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331740 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331743 13194139535108 true] [17592186331740 1110 #uuid "4031b93d-ce9f-5ee0-b4a2-e72bdb76b97c" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331741 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331741 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331741 1111 #uuid "c82fadb1-6b06-5934-a75c-e331b66e0c15" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331742 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331742 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331742 1111 #uuid "d3595b6a-4053-5bc5-97a6-7f2ffde489c0" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331743 1034 "1" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331743 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331743 1111 #uuid "a4287213-9eac-55f1-8d77-e28769b1a69c" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331744 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331744 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331744 1111 #uuid "ed6f3469-8b02-5bb6-a65a-4f5e928ba94c" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331745 1034 "\\frac{3}{8}" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331745 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331745 1111 #uuid "0e6058b3-deb7-5a21-a099-0317a2feaa64" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331746 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331747 13194139535108 true] [17592186331746 1089 "q-81243" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331746 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535108 true] [17592186331746 1100 "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[1,2]\\times [1,e].$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331746 1113 #uuid "1b17aeae-345a-5d7a-904d-6b5cb3dd86f7" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331746 1145 "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{3}{y}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{3}{y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}4{x}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3}{y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(2-1){\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{3}{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|]_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}4{x}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(e-1){\\int }_{1}^{2}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(e-1)[{x}^{4}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(e-1)({2}^{4}-{1}^{4}) \\\\  & =15(e-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A=3-15(e-1)=18-15e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331748 13194139535108 true] [17592186331747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331749 13194139535108 true] [17592186331747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331750 13194139535108 true] [17592186331747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331751 13194139535108 true] [17592186331747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331752 13194139535108 true] [17592186331747 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535108 true] [17592186331747 1041 "selection" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331747 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331749 13194139535108 true] [17592186331747 1110 #uuid "36835f30-7d82-5080-9230-15da409493fe" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331748 1034 "12-15e" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331748 1111 #uuid "988ee327-4bf2-5fbf-991c-51f874065693" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331749 1034 "18-15e" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331749 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331749 1111 #uuid "4841591a-03d2-5cfa-80af-80fbd0491d0a" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331750 1034 "18e-15" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331750 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331750 1111 #uuid "6f52f616-acc9-5cac-9997-a3db51a1ccca" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331751 1034 "15-12e" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331751 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331751 1111 #uuid "431fd19b-3d4d-5c5f-8063-f63b468621eb" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331752 1034 "15e-18" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331752 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331752 1111 #uuid "1215dade-8beb-59ba-8ed4-df07826cb508" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331753 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331754 13194139535108 true] [17592186331753 1089 "q-81245" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331753 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535108 true] [17592186331753 1100 "Calculate ${∬}_{R}(4{y}^{3}-2x)\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[2,5]\\times [0,3].$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331753 1113 #uuid "1adca866-e43f-5fb1-b3ea-e60c847c71ea" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331753 1145 "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(4{y}^{3}-2x)\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}4{y}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}2x\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}4{y}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(5-2){\\int }_{0}^{3}4{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3[{y}^{4}]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =3({3}^{4}-{0}^{4}) \\\\  & =243.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2x\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(3-0){\\int }_{2}^{5}2x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3[{x}^{2}]_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =3({5}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =63.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(4{y}^{3}-2x)\\,\\text{d}A=243-63=180.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331755 13194139535108 true] [17592186331754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331756 13194139535108 true] [17592186331754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331757 13194139535108 true] [17592186331754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331758 13194139535108 true] [17592186331754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331759 13194139535108 true] [17592186331754 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535108 true] [17592186331754 1041 "selection" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331754 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331755 13194139535108 true] [17592186331754 1110 #uuid "86a21dc0-883a-5e25-ac9f-03459c28f5b0" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331755 1034 "180" 13194139535108 true] [17592186331755 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535108 true] [17592186331755 1111 #uuid "4ae4fc5c-5552-5293-b8b8-3c55edfc9901" 1319413953